cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "phader: peptide insert counting for T7 phage display sequencing data"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Pleiko
    given-names: Karlis
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1073-197X"
repository-code: "https://github.com/KarlisPleiko/phader"
url: "https://github.com/KarlisPleiko/phader"
abstract: >-
  phader counts peptide inserts in next-generation sequencing reads from T7 phage
  display biopanning experiments. Reads are translated in all six frames, anchored on
  the constant leader sequence immediately upstream of the variable insert, and filtered
  by library scaffold (CX4C, CX7C, CX8C, CX10C, generic C...C, or an X7-TEV-His6
  cassette), read quality, NNK codon compatibility and optional peptide allow/deny lists.
  Identical peptides are tallied per input file and reported as a ranked count table,
  optionally with the underlying DNA variants clustered by a weighted edit distance to
  collapse sequencing errors. A Streamlit interface runs the analysis over a local
  directory of FASTQ/FASTA files without uploading them.
keywords:
  - phage display
  - T7 phage
  - biopanning
  - peptide library
  - next-generation sequencing
  - FASTQ
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
